  "goodToKnow": "Überaus means extremely or exceedingly: überaus freundlich, überaus erfolgreich. It's an elevated intensifier, typical of formal letters, speeches and newspapers; in everyday speech, Germans say sehr, total or echt. It's made of über (over) and aus (out): over and beyond. Similar formal intensifiers include äußerst, höchst and ungemein. Overusing überaus in casual talk can sound stiff or ironic."
